---
short_label: VIII.23
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If four numbers are in continued proportion, and the first is a cube, then the fourth is also a cube.
----
proof:

Let *A, B, C,* and *D* be four numbers in continued proportion, and let *A* be a cube.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="170" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VIII.23 diagram" src="propVIII23.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VIII.23",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "B0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,110;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,110;0;0",
            "D0;point;free;-1000,145;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;1000,145;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,90,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,30,0;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,115,0;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,30,0;0",
            "C2;point;proportion;A1,A2,B1,B2,B1,B2,C1,C3;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,30,0;0",
            "D2;point;proportion;A1,A2,B1,B2,C1,C2,D1,D3;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that *D* is also a cube.

Since between *A* and *D* there are two mean proportional numbers *B* and *C,* therefore *A* and *D* are similar solid numbers. But *A* is a cube, therefore *D* is also a cube. [!just VIII.21]

Therefore, *if four numbers are in continued proportion, and the first is a cube, then the fourth is also a cube.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
